   more is not licensed. Liquid AI, LFM and LFM3 are names of Liquid AI, Inc., used here only to describe the origin
   of the base model.

2. Wikidata (Wikimedia Foundation and contributors), CC0 1.0
   Item labels and descriptions, statements, external identifiers (IMDb, TMDB, TheTVDB and others) and official
   film ratings in the databases come from Wikidata (https://www.wikidata.org): collected through the Wikidata Query
   Service on 1 November 2026, and through the Wikidata API for titles added to Wikidata since then.

3. Wikipedia (Wikimedia Foundation and contributors), CC BY-SA 4.0 / CC BY-SA 3.0
   Lead and plot sections of English and German Wikipedia articles were part of the model input during training and
   scoring: current article text fetched through the MediaWiki API since October 2026, and the 1 November 2023 dump
   published as the Hugging Face dataset wikimedia/wikipedia. No Wikipedia text is included in the databases; the
   full database only stores the titles of the linked articles.

4. Rating systems
   FSK (Freiwillige Selbstkontrolle der Filmwirtschaft GmbH), MPA, BBFC, Kijkwijzer and the other rating systems are
   named only to identify where official ratings come from. They are not affiliated with this project and have not
   reviewed or endorsed any estimate. Besides the official ratings on Wikidata, the model was trained on 1,381 FSK
   ratings of TV shows read from German retailer, streaming and database websites (see model/README.md). These
   ratings are not included in the databases or in this repository.

5. Python packages used by the pipeline (pipeline/requirements.txt) are installed separately and not
   redistributed: PyTorch, Transformers, PEFT, safetensors, huggingface_hub, NumPy, pandas, PyArrow, scikit-learn,
   mwparserfromhell.
